:{"@id":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/"}},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/#\/schema\/person\/05fd1aef04d178f2231400ddb85550a2","name":"KrakenFX","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/16c47affada0c14e53e9e35216ec483ad12bcc35fd4cea0d6a2dd22cde9a6038?s=96&d=identicon&r=g","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/16c47affada0c14e53e9e35216ec483ad12bcc35fd4cea0d6a2dd22cde9a6038?s=96&d=identicon&r=g","contentUrl":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/16c47affada0c14e53e9e35216ec483ad12bcc35fd4cea0d6a2dd22cde9a6038?s=96&d=identicon&r=g","caption":"KrakenFX"},"url":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/author\/danielpintokraken"}]}},"jetpack_likes_enabled":false,"jetpack_sharing_enabled":true,"jetpack_shortlink":"https:\/\/wp.me\/peDd1v-4y8","jetpack_featured_media_url":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/02\/blog_header-4-1.png?fit=3072%2C1400&ssl=1","_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/17492","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/230089380"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=17492"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/17492\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":27731,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/17492\/revisions\/27731"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/17528"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=17492"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=17492"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=17492"},{"taxonomy":"language","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/language?post=17492"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":17402,"date":"2023-02-02T19:23:38","date_gmt":"2023-02-03T00:23:38","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/?p=17402"},"modified":"2023-05-08T16:37:53","modified_gmt":"2023-05-08T20:37:53","slug":"crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial-crypto-wallets","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/crypto-education\/crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial-crypto-wallets","title":{"rendered":"Crypto 101: What are custodial and non-custodial crypto wallets?"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Wallets play a foundational role in crypto security and, depending on which option you choose, can often be the difference between keeping or losing funds in certain situations.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">There are two main types of crypto wallets you\u2019ll need to consider:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Custodial<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Non-custodial<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Each option has advantages and disadvantages and suits different needs depending on your investment goals, technical experience, and risk tolerance.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">In the latest article from the Kraken Learn Center, we break down the details of each of these wallet options so you can make a more informed decision about how you choose to keep your crypto safe. Check out one of our latest articles to get all the details you need.<\/span><\/p>\n<div style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" style=\"display: inline-block; padding: 12px 32px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; text-decoration: none; transition: opacity 0.2s linear 0s; line-height: 24px; border-radius: 90px; color: #ffffff; background-color: #5d45dc; border: 1px solid #5D45DC;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.kraken.com\/learn\/custodial-non-custodial-crypto-wallet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn more<\/a><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">\u00a0<\/span><\/div>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">The key defining characteristic between a custodial and a non-custodial crypto wallet is who ultimately controls the private keys to it.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">With custodial wallets,\u00a0<\/span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">a third party manages<\/span><\/strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">\u00a0the private keys. This involves placing trust in an intermediary, such as a cryptocurrency exchange like Kraken, to secure your funds on your behalf.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">With non-custodial wallets, the responsibility of storing and securing the private keys lies solely\u00a0<\/span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">with the wallet owner<\/span><\/strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">. If you opt to secure your assets, you must shoulder the burden of ensuring they\u2019re properly stored and protected against cyber and physical threats alone.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Ultimately, when it comes to choosing between custodial and non-custodial wallets you\u2019ll need to weigh what\u2019s most important to you; convenience or security.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">If the former, then custodial options like holding crypto on Kraken are perhaps better. If the latter is more important, then a hardware wallet device or web-based non-custodial solution is likely a better option.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Have more questions about the difference between custodial and non-custodial crypto wallets? Want to learn more about the pros and cons of both options? Need more details on how to keep your crypto safe?<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Check out the latest article from the Kraken Learn Center\u00a0<\/span><a class=\"editor-rtfLink\" href=\"https:\/\/www.kraken.com\/learn\/custodial-non-custodial-crypto-wallet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">What are custodial and non-custodial crypto wallets?<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<div style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; text-align: center;\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" style=\"display: inline-block; padding: 12px 32px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; text-decoration: none; transition: opacity 0.2s linear 0s; line-height: 24px; border-radius: 90px; color: #ffffff; background-color: #5d45dc; border: 1px solid #5D45DC;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.kraken.com\/learn\/custodial-non-custodial-crypto-wallet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn more<\/a><\/div>\n<hr \/>\n<p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These materials are for general information purposes only and are not investment advice or a recommendation or solicitation to buy, sell, or hold any digital asset or to engage in any specific trading strategy. Some crypto products and markets are unregulated, and you may not be protected by government compensation and\/or regulatory protection schemes. The unpredictable nature of the cryptoasset markets can lead to loss of funds. Tax may be payable on any return and\/or on any increase in the value of your crypto assets and you should seek independent advice on your taxation position.<\/span><\/i><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Wallets play a foundational role in crypto security and, depending on which option you choose, can often be the difference between keeping or losing funds in certain situations. There are two main types of crypto wallets you\u2019ll need to consider: Custodial Non-custodial Each option has advantages and disadvantages and suits different needs depending on your [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":120066484,"featured_media":16424,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_jetpack_newsletter_access":"","_jetpack_dont_email_post_to_subs":false,"_jetpack_newsletter_tier_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paywalled_content":false,"_wpcom_ai_launchpad_first_post":false,"_jetpack_feature_clip_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paid_content":false,"footnotes":"","jetpack_post_was_ever_published":false},"categories":[1391],"tags":[],"language":[],"class_list":["post-17402","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-crypto-education"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v23.2 (Yoast SEO v28.5) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-premium-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Crypto 101: What are custodial and non-custodial crypto wallets? - Kraken Blog<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/crypto-education\/crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial-crypto-wallets\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Crypto 101: What are custodial and non-custodial crypto wallets?\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Wallets play a foundational role in crypto security and, depending on which option you choose, can often be the difference between keeping or losing funds in certain situations. There are two main types of crypto wallets you\u2019ll need to consider: Custodial Non-custodial Each option has advantages and disadvantages and suits different needs depending on your [&hellip;]\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/blog.kraken.com\/crypto-education\/crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial-crypto-wallets\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Kraken Blog\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2023-02-03T00:23:38+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2023-05-08T20:37:53+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/blog.kraken.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/Blog-Inner-Self-custody-best-practices.png?fit=1536%2C700&ssl=1\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1536\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"700\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image\/png\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"krakenfx\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"krakenfx\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\\/\\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/crypto-education\\\/crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial-crypto-wallets#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/crypto-education\\\/crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial-crypto-wallets\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"krakenfx\",\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/#\\\/schema\\\/person\\\/461b7fbe1832d96cab8eb182c6642a21\"},\"headline\":\"Crypto 101: What are custodial and non-custodial crypto wallets?\",\"datePublished\":\"2023-02-03T00:23:38+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2023-05-08T20:37:53+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\\/\\\/blog.kraken.com\\\/crypto-education\\\/crypto-101-what-are-custodial-and-non-custodial